WEBVTT

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.990
The god of thunder
will steal my belly button!

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:46.040
KAGUYA WANTS TO GIVE A GIFT

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.620
You're that afraid of thunder?

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.790
After all, it suddenly goes crack
and then boom!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.830
I hate loud noises!

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.630
Then why not cover your ears?

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:54.840
If I cover my ears, then my hands
aren't free to protect my belly button!

00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:01.180
I'd think that'd be obvious! I'd think
that'd be obvious! I'd think that'd be obvious!

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.760
<i>What does "obvious" mean again?</i>

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.310
Obvious.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.890
I'm protecting my belly button,
so please cover my ears, Miss Kaguya.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.440
S-Sure.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.690
OBVIOUS

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:14.690
The trains are stopped
because of the typhoon!

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.450
That's a pain. You'd better call home.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.030
We don't have a car,
so there's nothing they can do about it.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.740
What am I gonna do?

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:28.580
<i>That's right.
I can just give him a lift home.</i>

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.580
SHUCHIIN ACADEMY
(MINATO WARD)

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.580
SHIROGANE'S HOUSE
(SETAGAYA WARD)

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:30.790
President, if you like...

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.840
<i>Huh? That'd make it a driving date!</i>

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:39.090
<i>Going for a drive!
That is definitely a kind of date.</i>

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.640
<i>Sitting shoulder to shoulder
in an enclosed space,</i>

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.220
<i>listening to pleasant music on the radio</i>

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.100
<i>and chatting while cruising
through town in the rain.</i>

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.480
<i>And at red lights...</i>

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.770
<i>I wish this light
would never change to green.</i>

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.110
<i>...is the kind of thing they would think.</i>

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.780
<i>Strictly speaking, the presence of Kaguya's
driver would mean the two weren't alone,</i>

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:02.870
<i>but basically, to her, it would be
a prime example of a driving date.</i>

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.330
<i>Thus...</i>

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.160
Ow! That hurts!

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:10.660
<i>It's like I'm asking him out on a date!</i>

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:13.080
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:12.210
What's wrong, Shinomiya?

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.080
Nothing.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.170
It's nothing.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.590
<i>If the president brought it up,
that's one thing,</i>

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.220
<i>but I can't afford to make the offer.</i>

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:21.470
<i>And yet,</i>

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.850
<i>abandoning him to his own devices
when he has no way to get home would be...</i>

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:30.310
<i>That's it! There's no problem
if he just says, "Give me a ride."</i>

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.480
My taxi is almost here.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:37.190
Oh, really?

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.900
What should I do?

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:39.820
Huh?

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:42.400
The president doesn't have a ride home?

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.280
L-Looks like it.

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.030
Then why don't we share the—

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.700
I just saw a flash of lightning.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.870
I'll cover your ears tight
so you don't hear the thunder.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.540
Thank you.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.090
I'll cover your eyes, too, while I'm at it.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.670
Why?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.550
Now, I'll escort you to your taxi like this.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:01.590
Wait!

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:02.930
Miss Kaguya!

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:05.260
I'm scared! I'm scared!

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.350
But it's kind of fun!

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.310
What kind of game is that?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:18.320
<i>With the element of chaos out of the way,
no one's left to interfere.</i>

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.570
<i>But how can I get him to say,
"Give me a ride"?</i>

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.320
Crap, I have to work today.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.280
At this rate, I'll miss my shift.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.830
Indeed.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.950
Taking off work because of a typhoon

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.960
would disqualify one
as a member of society.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.630
Paying a taxi fare to get there
even though it'd cost more than daily wages,

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:39.210
or someone giving them a ride...

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.630
To a member of society,
the choice would be clear, you know?

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.090
<i>That was effective.</i>

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.560
I'm going to the restroom
and will think along the way!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.100
Go right ahead.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.850
<i>It's hard to imagine the president
taking a taxi, cheapskate that he is.</i>

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.860
<i>So, naturally,
he'll come groveling to me.</i>

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:59.320
IT'D PROBABLY BE AROUND 5,000 YEN...

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.110
<i>I have this victory in the bag.</i>

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:06.570
<i>5,000 yen.</i>

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.620
<i>I make 1,000 an hour,
so that's five hours of work.</i>

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.580
<i>But I'd hate to miss it.</i>

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.960
TRAIN OPERATING
TRAIN OPERATING
TRAIN DELAYED
TRAIN OPERATING

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.960
<i>Huh? The trains
are running again!</i>

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.670
<i>Why now, of all times?</i>

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.090
<i>Pour it on a little harder, typhoon!</i>

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.840
<i>This leaves me no choice.</i>

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.350
THE SEVEN ANTI-SHIROGANE TOOLS
TOOL ONE

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.350
RECHARGEABLE
BATTERY IS DEAD

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:28.510
<i>Number one of the Seven
Anti-Shirogane Tools!</i>

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.350
<i>A dead battery!</i>

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.220
<i>Anticipating a variety of situations,</i>

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.100
<i>Kaguya has prepared a number of items
to take down Shirogane.</i>

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.350
<i>This dead rechargeable battery
is one of them!</i>

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.360
<i>I have about a minute before the president
returns from the restroom. During that time,</i>

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.530
<i>I'll switch out his phone battery!</i>

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.450
<i>There isn't much time.</i>

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.620
<i>Level of difficulty is very hard.</i>

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.240
<i>But I have confidence in myself!</i>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:07.630
What's the matter, Shinomiya?

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.930
N-Nothing. I was just doing
a little light exercise.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.020
My battery's dead?

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.150
Hey, Shinomiya, can I borrow—

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:22.400
L-Looks like my ride's here, too,
so I'd better get going!

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:23.690
R-Right.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.070
See you tomorrow.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:36.250
<i>Now I just need to wait here.</i>

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.210
<i>Shinomiya, you're getting a ride home?</i>

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.960
<i>Please! Give me a ride!</i>

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.170
<i>Well, I can hardly refuse
if you're reduced to begging me.</i>

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.970
<i>Poor President, I'll give you a lift home.</i>

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.300
<i>You're a goddess!</i>

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:56.850
Um, Lady Kaguya, it's a cute scheme,

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.850
but if it works,
how am I supposed to get home?

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:01.850
On foot.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:02.980
Are you a demon?

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.270
If you don't take better care of me,

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.400
karma will take a bite
out of your ass one day.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.530
Oh, you and your karma...

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:23.330
See?

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.460
I was kidding.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:29.380
I already called a taxi
for you, Hayasaka.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.850
Jeez!

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.110
Well,

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.990
I figured this would happen, too.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:54.490
Then, you should've stopped me before.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.830
I'll take off school today, too.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.580
I'll go make you some porridge.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.380
No, stay by my side, Hayasaka.

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.420
I wish you were always this adorable.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.920
Apparently, Shinomiya has a cold.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.890
<i>This will continue
in the Heart-pounding Visit chapter.</i>

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:19.220
<i>Very nice. I love how you can do
so many things with it!</i>

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:19.930
SHIROGANE GOT A NEW BATTERY
FOR HIS (USED, NO WARRANTY) PHONE

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.690
Apparently, Shinomiya has a cold.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.900
So, somebody's supposed to deliver
handouts to her house.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:28.650
CHIKA FUJIWARA
WANTS TO PAY A VISIT

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.230
Me! I'll go!

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:30.400
Fujiwara?

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.820
I've visited her at home
when she was sick once before,

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:39.290
and it's hilarious how much of a baby
Miss Kaguya becomes when she has a cold!

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:39.290
GRIN

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:40.950
<i>A baby?</i>

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:43.080
<i>President, dry my back.</i>

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.330
She's so cute!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:48.170
GLOW GLOW

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:50.460
It's the one time you can snatch her up
in a bear hug and she won't get angry!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.550
<i>President, I need a hug.</i>

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.970
It wouldn't be fair if one person
got to monopolize her on her sickbed.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.760
So let's all go together!

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:01.100
All?

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:01.930
Yes!

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:06.350
Wouldn't a crowd barging in on a sick person
show lack of common sense?

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.860
I think one person would be plenty.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.190
TERRIFIED

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.190
<i>I don't wanna go because I'm scared.</i>

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.530
Good point.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:14.700
Then, who'll go?

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.450
Let's play Concentration to decide!

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:19.700
CONCENTRATION

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.700
<i>Concentration!</i>

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.450
<i>Needless to say,
a game that needs no introduction.</i>

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.160
We won't use the jokers.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:28.380
And if anyone's caught cheating,
they get minus five points.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.460
We'll see who's first
with rock-paper-scissors.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:35.630
All right, we'll start with the president!

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.300
Then, let's begin!

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:40.550
Hold your horses, Fujiwara!

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:43.310
Wh-Wh-What is it, President?

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:47.060
There are a number of points
I'm not clear about.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.900
First, the fact that you challenged us
to a memory game.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.820
I don't quite get that.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.440
Normally, I'd think you'd choose
a game you were actually good at.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.490
And you breezed through this rule,

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.820
but minus five points for cheating?

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.830
Not instant disqualification?

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.620
That made me wary.

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.210
I may not have noticed
if you'd kept your mouth shut,

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:11.960
but these designs
kinda look like numbers.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.340
This is a marked deck!

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.590
It really is!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.850
Fujiwara-senpai, that's low! Underhanded!

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.600
And getting caught
by the gambit you relied on!

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.560
That's the most embarrassing thing!

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.560
I'm embarrassed for you!
I'm going home!

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:38.860
Shame, shame, shame, shame,
shame, shame, shame, shame...

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.110
That's enough, Ishigami.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:37.240
We accepted her rule about cheating
which this surely would've fallen under.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.860
We only touched the deck, so we're fine.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:43.580
That's right! It's only cheating
if you get caught! Nyah!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.370
No, you certainly got caught.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:48.540
<i>Getting back on track...</i>

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.630
<i>In the first half of the game,</i>

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:54.710
<i>these flawed, but talented students
remembered the position of each card.</i>

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:57.630
<i>As the game proceeded,
they earned points, making no mistakes.</i>

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:02.430
<i>Shirogane, 10 points.
Fujiwara, 8 points. Ishigami, 10 points.</i>

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.140
<i>There were 24 cards left.</i>

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.390
Now I'm tied with you, Ishigami.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.900
<i>President, wipe my front, too.</i>

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:16.110
You guys have really good memories.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.690
I'm gonna raise the bar a bit!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:19.360
What?

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:21.200
<i>Mixing them up!</i>

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:26.490
<i>An extremely annoying strategy to destroy
their memories of the cards' positions.</i>

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.290
MIXING THE CARDS

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:29.330
<i>Crap! I can't remember which is which!</i>

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:33.670
<i>After moving the cards around,
Fujiwara smoothly won several points,</i>

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.790
<i>even making up
for the penalty for cheating!</i>

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.130
Let's enjoy the rest of the game, you guys!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.930
<i>Uh-oh. I'm in last place!</i>

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.050
SHIROGANE: 10
FUJIWARA: 18 (-5)
ISHIGAMI: 12

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.050
CARDS REMAINING: 12

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:48.310
<i>At this rate, I won't be able to see
Shinomiya acting like a baby!</i>

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.560
<i>President, pet my head.</i>

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.860
What should I bring her?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.070
She almost never gets sick,
so this is a rare opportunity!

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:01.950
Well, I'm not surprised she got a cold
after being drenched like that.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:06.160
Shinomiya got drenched?
She got a ride home, didn't she?

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:08.580
Beats me. I just know
what I happened to see.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:17.130
She was in front of the school gate
waiting for someone, I suppose.

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.130
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:23.550
<i>she was waiting for me?</i>

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.260
<i>There's no definite proof.</i>

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.310
<i>If it was me...</i>

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:32.310
<i>Then, never mind
Shinomiya acting like a baby.</i>

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.400
<i>I'm an idiot for thinking
about nothing but silly things!</i>

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.360
<i>I'm the one who needs
to visit her at home!</i>

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:42.570
<i>Use your head for something
other than fantasizing about nonsense!</i>

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:44.200
13.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:47.370
<i>13! Damn it! The matching card
appeared a minute ago!</i>

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.910
<i>Is she gonna get this one, too?</i>

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.330
Nope.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.500
<i>Was it just a mistake?</i>

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.180
<i>No, wait.</i>

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.350
<i>I see.</i>

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.890
It's your turn, President!

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:14.640
I got it!

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:14.890
SHIROGANE: 10

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:15.190
SHIROGANE: 12

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:15.940
I got it!

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:16.190
SHIROGANE: 12

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:16.480
SHIROGANE: 14

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:17.060
SHIROGANE: 14

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:18.310
I got it!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:17.730
SHIROGANE: 16

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:18.310
SHIROGANE: 18

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:21.730
I win.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:25.490
FINAL SCORE:
1ST PLACE - SHIROGANE: 18
2ND PLACE - FUJIWARA: 18 (-5)
3RD PLACE - ISHIGAMI: 16

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.490
<i>Shirogane took first place.</i>

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:28.740
That was some comeback.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.950
Well, if you know the trick, it's a cinch.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:32.870
Trick?

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:38.580
The unusual thing about these cards
is that the patterns aren't symmetrical,

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:41.210
so you can use them like this.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:46.470
I see!

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.970
The hands on a clock!

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:49.970
That's right.
By placing the cards at an angle,

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.600
you can reveal their face values
from 1 to 12.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:55.810
So, Fujiwara wanted to place
the 13 cards far away

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.310
since they didn't figure into her plan.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:00.730
Moving the cards around
was also done to hide her trick.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.940
Fujiwara-senpai...

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:07.740
That's low!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.700
Underhanded! Playing dirty!
You haven't learned your lesson at all!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.740
You're shameless!
How did you get to be so shameless?

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:17.410
The most shameful thing is how he won
by finding your method and using it himself!

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:21.000
For shame!
Again, shame on you, Fujiwara-senpai!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.170
Don't look at me!

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:25.630
A-After all... After all...

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.800
I just wanted to visit her at home!

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:31.760
I wanna die, so I'm going home.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.430
Is that right?

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.310
But please don't die on us!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.860
Even though it worked on my sisters...

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.820
Can you believe her brass?

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:47.820
This just goes to show
how shallow analog gamers are!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.820
It's like she dug herself into a hole!

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:53.450
<i>This happens when you do something
that doesn't suit you.</i>

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.950
<i>Shinomiya wouldn't have gotten
tripped up like that.</i>

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.250
<i>Shinomiya would have...</i>

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:02.540
<i>Crap! Now I'm nervous!</i>

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.210
<i>What should I bring her?</i>

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:10.340
I wanna eat canned peaches, Hayasaka.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.760
Yes, yes.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:15.970
<i>The Heart-pounding Visit
continues to Part Two.</i>

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:15.970
WHAT DO YOU GIVE A RICH PERSON?

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:24.570
RESULTS OF TODAY'S MATCH:

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:24.570
FAILURE

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:24.570
SINCE NEITHER OF THEM
HAD A STRATEGY

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.200
<i>This is the famous Shinomiya Villa!</i>

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:35.990
<i>I saw it online before,
but up close, it's amazing!</i>

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:39.710
Maybe I should've done more
than bring drinks and jello.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:46.750
I have been appointed to the role
of Lady Kaguya's caretaker.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.380
My name is Smithee A. Herthaka.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.260
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.390
COLOR CONTACTS

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:56.140
STUFFED A BIT

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.140
<i>A maid!</i>

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:03.900
I assume you have come
to visit Lady Kaguya.

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:05.360
ABOUT KAGUYA SHINOMIYA,
PART 1

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.190
Yes, exactly!

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.820
Then, I'll show you to her room.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.070
Um, actually...

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:14.530
I'm only here
to deliver handouts to Shinomiya!

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:17.450
I was thinking you could
give it to her, Miss Herthaka!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.160
Don't chicken out after coming this far.

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:23.790
Right this way.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.210
Yes, but...

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:29.590
Honestly, I think it would be best
if you gave it to Lady Kaguya directly.

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:30.380
But...

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:33.720
Lady Kaguya...

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.800
you have a visitor.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.890
Hey! What are you doing, Lady Kaguya?

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.060
Messy!

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.900
But I can't find them.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.070
What are you looking for?

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:49.320
Fireworks.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:50.320
Fireworks?

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:53.200
You'll do them with me,
won't you, Hayasaka?

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.820
I certainly will not.

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:59.790
Summer is around the corner.
I can understand why you'd jump the gun.

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:01.620
Your priority is to recover from this cold.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:05.460
Meanie! I wanna do fireworks!

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:07.790
That aside, you have a visitor.

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:10.000
A visitor?

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:17.720
President!

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.100
What are you doing here, President?

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.350
Well, um...

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:25.020
Are you living here from now on?
I didn't hear about that!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.730
No! I'm not moving in!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.610
Miss Herthaka, what's wrong with her?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.780
According to Sigmund Freud,

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:34.780
human actions are determined
by one's desire, the id,

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:37.620
ID (DESIRE)

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.620
and one's reason, the ego.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:37.620
EGO (REASON)

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.240
I WANT TO SLEEP

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.330
Human instincts produce
the desires of the id

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:42.870
I WANT TO PUNCH

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:46.170
while it's the duty of the ego to act
as a brake that suppresses those desires.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.080
I WANT TO EAT

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:45.250
I WANT TO PLAY

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:49.500
However, if the ability to think,

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.670
which is the source of the ego,
is lost for some reason,

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.510
the person becomes a beast
that acts according to the id.

00:17:57.010 --> 00:17:59.300
In other words,
the person becomes a simpleton.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.050
A simpleton?

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:03.350
And for people whose brains
are normally in full gear,

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.680
the effect is markedly pronounced.

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.440
At a glance, it looks like she's awake,

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.570
but she's actually in the middle
of a fever dream.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:15.030
Once she's on her feet,

00:18:15.030 --> 00:18:18.660
she'll have no memory at all
of the time she was sick.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.530
It's as if she were drunk.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.490
<i>This is getting strange again.</i>

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:26.160
Well, I need to get back to work,

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.000
so please keep Lady Kaguya company.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.290
Understood.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:36.420
Listen, I can assure you no one will enter
this room during the next three hours,

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:39.430
but you mustn't do anything inappropriate.

00:18:39.640 --> 00:18:41.680
I-I won't.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:45.270
On top of that,
this room is soundproofed,

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.140
and Lady Kaguya will have
no recollection of your visit.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.560
So no matter what you do,
no one will be the wiser,

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:52.650
but absolutely...

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:56.440
do not do anything inappropriate.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:57.950
I said I wouldn't!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:10.460
Shinomiya, I bought you
a variety of drinks.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:11.830
Want one?

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:14.090
Fireworks?

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.960
No, they're not fireworks.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:17.340
<i>It's useless.</i>

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.970
<i>Shinomiya isn't even in a state
to have a conversation.</i>

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:25.430
<i>If I'm honest with myself, my filthy mind
was hoping I could help her drink it,</i>

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:27.730
<i>but she's much weaker
than I anticipated.</i>

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:30.600
<i>If I take advantage of this,</i>

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:34.020
<i>I might be able to get Shinomiya's
true feelings and weaknesses out of her.</i>

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:34.980
<i>However...</i>

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:41.360
Shinomiya, is it my fault
you caught this cold?

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:45.990
You intended to give me a ride
yesterday, didn't you?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:49.250
And you were waiting
at the school gate, which is when...

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.580
I don't know.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:55.750
I kinda feel like that's right,
and I kinda feel like that's wrong.

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.250
Well, which is it?

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.510
President, are you mad?

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.930
I'm sorry.

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:05.260
No, you didn't say anything
to make me mad.

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.760
No.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.270
I'm always doing things
that make trouble for you.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.400
I never know what to do.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.440
For so many things,

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:22.030
it's the first time for me,
so I don't know.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:27.540
IF YOU ARE A SHINOMIYA,
DO NOT RELY ON ANYONE. INSTEAD, USE THEM.
DO NOT RECEIVE ANYTHING. INSTEAD, STEAL.
DO NOT LOVE ANYONE. THERE IS NO INSTEAD.

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:24.030
So,

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:27.540
all I can do is behave the way I know how.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.080
I don't know any other ways.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.420
This is the only way I can do it.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.170
So, for today...

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.430
let's sleep together.

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:46.430
No, Shinomiya!

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.600
Are you shy?

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:54.310
How cute.

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:55.560
<i>Wait a second!</i>

00:20:55.810 --> 00:21:00.320
<i>Shinomiya will forget this, too,
and no one will come into the room?</i>

00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:02.740
<i>This situation
is just too convenient!</i>

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:05.570
<i>And I'm not confident
that I can control myself!</i>

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:07.580
<i>What the hell...</i>

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:12.750
<i>has happened to me?</i>

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:13.960
ID AND EGO

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:18.090
SLEEP DEPRIVED

00:21:27.140 --> 00:21:28.970
What time is it?

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.850
Feels like I've just come out of hibernation.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.200
President?

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:46.410
What were you doing in my bed?

00:21:46.410 --> 00:21:48.620
I-I just came over to visit you!

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:52.240
What kinda man takes the opportunity
to crawl into bed? Unbelievable!

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:53.620
You invited me!

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:57.000
In your dreams! How could you
do it when I was sleeping!

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.540
You're scum!
Get out of here right now!

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:06.090
Oh, dear. I thought
something like this might happen.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:12.100
But it looks like you're well rested anyway.

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:14.230
H-Hayasaka,

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:16.600
how far did I go with the president?

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:17.980
I couldn't say.

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:19.980
Even after...

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:23.360
Even after I totally held back!
I held back for all I was worth!

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:26.490
<i>The Heart-pounding Visit: The End.</i>

00:22:26.490 --> 00:22:29.990
Well, I guess nothing happened.
